{"name":"Late Bloomer","hex":"#db8959","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"late bloomer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who reaches puberty or who matures comparatively later than is typical.","A person who enters a romantic relationship or engages in sexual intercourse significantly later in life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/late_bloomer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Late Bloomers (2006 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Late Bloomers is a 2006 Swiss German-language comedy film directed by Bettina Oberli and starring Stephanie Glaser. It follows an elderly seamstress who opens a lingerie boutique in her Emmental village, causing unrest. The film was Switzerland's submission for the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film at the 80th Academy Awards, and Annemarie Düringer won Best Actress at the Geneva International Film Festival in 2006."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Bloomers_(2006_film)","wikidata":"Q627327"},{"title":"Late Bloomers (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Late Bloomers is a 2011 romantic comedy-drama film directed by Julie Gavras and starring William Hurt and Isabella Rossellini. The film premiered on 18 February 2011 at the 61st Berlin International Film Festival. It was released theatrically in France on 13 July 2011 by Gaumont."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/Late_Bloomers_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Bloomers_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q6495199"},{"title":"Late bloomer","blocks":[{"text":"A late bloomer is a person whose talents or capabilities are not visible to others until later than usual. The term is used metaphorically to describe a child or adolescent who develops slower than others in their age group, but eventually catches up and in some cases overtakes their peers, or an adult whose talent or genius in a particular field only appears later in life than is normal – in some cases only in old age."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_bloomer","wikidata":"Q2210924"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Young_Thomas_Edison.jpg/500px-Young_Thomas_Edison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Young_Thomas_Edison.jpg/500px-Young_Thomas_Edison.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thomas Edison as a boy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung_Thomas_Edison.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Albert_Einstein_as_a_child.jpg/500px-Albert_Einstein_as_a_child.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Albert_Einstein_as_a_child.jpg/500px-Albert_Einstein_as_a_child.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albert Einstein in 1893 (age 14)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbert_Einstein_as_a_child.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/William_Butler_Yeats_by_John_Butler_Yeats_1900.jpg/330px-William_Butler_Yeats_by_John_Butler_Yeats_1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/William_Butler_Yeats_by_John_Butler_Yeats_1900.jpg/330px-William_Butler_Yeats_by_John_Butler_Yeats_1900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Portrait of young William Butler Yeats by his father, John Butler Yeats","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliam_Butler_Yeats_by_John_Butler_Yeats_1900.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Grandma_Moses_NYWTS.jpg/500px-Grandma_Moses_NYWTS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&